# promise: crash-sign-in-dialog-tab-closed
# A tab closed while its page's HTTP sign-in prompt is up (a router or intranet page left asking for a
# user name and password). Cra's host for page dialogs (cra-page-dialogs.patch) told the prompt its host
# was going only as the page's own data was torn down, the last step of closing it; Chrome then shut
# the prompt at once, and its sign-in handler, already gone with the page's request, was used anyway:
# SIGSEGV in LoginHandler::CancelAuth (0.1.50 and 0.1.51 crash reports). The host now lets its dialogs go
# when the page starts closing, while all of it is still there.
budget rss=900 stalls50=30
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=before
wait 1
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/auth?n=closed-tab
expect-log "GET /auth\?n=closed-tab HTTP/1.1" 401
wait 2
cra://debug?pageDialogs=sign-in
expect-log page dialog sign-in: chrome [0-9]+x[0-9]+ at=page front=1 .*buttons=.*Cancel.* fields=2
cra://action/closeTab
wait 2
cra://debug?pageDialogs=after
expect-log page dialogs after: n=0
cra://debug?back=after
expect-log back after: selected=.*page\.html\?n=before
reject-log fault:
